// Host-specific niri config for hero — see niri.host.naut-dt.kdl for
// how the include is wired; this file exists so the "niri.host.kdl"
// include resolves (a new desktop host must commit its tail BEFORE the
// first switch or HM links against nothing).
//
// The desk: the 4K main with the 1440p VERTICAL on its LEFT. Output
// blocks belong in niri.outputs.kdl keyed by connector — add them once
// the machine reports its names (`niri msg outputs`); until then every
// monitor auto-places. Nothing monitor-specific lives here yet.

// the animated middle layer, replayed from the last look's recorded
// choice (mpvpaper:toggle persists on/off — see niri.nix). The video
// itself (~/Pictures/Wallpapers/live/spaceman.mp4) was machine-local
// on the predecessor desk and is NOT in the repo — until a copy lands
// at that path, an "on" replay starts mpvpaper which exits instantly:
// harmless, and the static wallpaper shows.
spawn-at-startup "sh" "-c" "mpvpaper:toggle \"$(cat ~/.local/state/desk-mpvpaper 2>/dev/null || echo off)\""
